WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for the silent Tally demo. The recording has no audio, so these
describe what is on screen rather than transcribing speech. They are the only
channel the video has: it autoplays muted, which is the one way a browser will
autoplay at all, so a visitor who does not read these sees pictures and no
argument.

Times are media time. The player applies a slower rate to the Activity and
Automations chapters, and the browser scales cue timing with playback rate, so
these stay in sync and those cues get longer on screen rather than shorter.

